# Family Hearth

This package is the Netlify-hosted family website named **The Calder Hearth** (`apps/family-hearth`).

- Keep copy warm, specific, and unhurried. Avoid corporate SaaS language.
- Preserve the ember-and-paper palette (`#1c1410`, `#f4ead8`, `#c45c26`, `#d4a056`).
- Routes are in-app views in `apps/family-hearth/src/App.jsx`: home, recipes, gatherings, stories, rsvp.
- Recipe, gathering, and story content lives in `apps/family-hearth/src/data.js`. Edit there, not as one-off JSX strings.
- The RSVP form must stay compatible with Netlify Forms (`name="family-rsvp"`, matching fields in `index.html`).
- Do not add backend databases unless explicitly requested. Static content plus Netlify Forms is the stack.
